import Wikipedia.HopfProblem.PeriodFamilyHigherDirectImageFibreKernel

/-!
# Genuine degree-one higher-direct-image stalk evaluation

Original period-character extension classes give actual stalk germs
whose fibre coordinates are the unchanged negative Dolbeault marking.
The evaluation map is surjective, with explicit additive lifts of every
original fibre cohomology class. On every open complex base it also has
an explicitly constructed nonzero kernel element.

These theorems do not assert local freeness of the higher direct image.
The expected base-change isomorphism requires specialization of its
original base-function module to the residue field, not the raw stalk.
-/
